From 0a1327fc6e97392087a81e43c122ad0625a22177 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matterward Labs <admin@matterwardlabs.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 20:49:42 +0530
Subject: keep .kotlin_module files in turbine header jars
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The kotlin-jar merge filters to .class entries only, which discards
META-INF/main.kotlin_module — the file that maps packages to their file
facades. Without it kotlinc resolves a dependency's Kotlin classes but none
of its top-level declarations: every cross-target extension function or
top-level composable fails as an unresolved reference while the facade class
sits on the classpath with complete metadata. Isolated outside the build:
the same probe compiles against the pre-merge ABI jar, fails against the
merged header jar, and passes again with the one entry restored. Upstream
has not hit this because no upstream Kotlin target consumes another's
top-level API through a header jar.

Specified by
chromium/patches/0013-keep-kotlin-module-files-in-turbine-header-jars.md.

Taffy-Patch: 0013

diff --git a/build/android/gyp/turbine.py b/build/android/gyp/turbine.py
index 07babde5e93e3..a69a0368bb27c 100755
--- a/build/android/gyp/turbine.py
+++ b/build/android/gyp/turbine.py
@@ -158,7 +158,14 @@ def main(argv):
     logging.info('Header compilation took %ss', end)
     if options.kotlin_jar_path:
       with zipfile.ZipFile(output_jar.name, 'a') as out_zip:
-        path_transform = lambda p: p if p.endswith('.class') else None
+        # META-INF/*.kotlin_module must survive alongside the classes: it maps
+        # packages to their file facades, and without it kotlinc cannot
+        # resolve a dependency's top-level Kotlin declarations (functions,
+        # properties) even though the facade classes and their metadata are
+        # all present. Dropping it breaks any Kotlin target that consumes
+        # another Kotlin target's top-level API through this header jar.
+        path_transform = lambda p: p if p.endswith('.class') or p.endswith(
+            '.kotlin_module') else None
         zip_helpers.merge_zips(out_zip, [options.kotlin_jar_path],
                                path_transform=path_transform)
 
